# gitleaksignore — baseline of pre-existing findings.
#
# These fingerprints were flagged by gitleaks on the working tree as of the
# chore/add-gitleaks-secret-scanning PR. They are intentionally ignored here
# so CI does not fail on legacy issues, while still failing on any *new*
# secret introduced after this baseline.
#
# Categories of entries below:
#
# 1. Private-key placeholder markers in docs (false positives).
#    Examples: `-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----`.
#
# 2. A hard-coded `admin-key` value in admin portal pages and test scripts.
#    These look like a real ADMIN_API_KEY shipped to the client. They need
#    a proper fix in a follow-up PR — move the call through a server route
#    (or NEXT_PUBLIC env at minimum), rotate the existing key, and remove
#    these entries from this file.
#
# To regenerate after fixing app code:
#   pnpm run security:scan --report-path /tmp/leaks.json
#   then re-derive fingerprints from /tmp/leaks.json.

